mission impossible fallout runs for an  amazing 147 minutes and is jam-packed  with awesome action scenes and stunning  moments but there were even more great  scenes cut from the final movie yippie  Kay may be lovers it's Jan here and in  this video I'm revealing the top 10  deleted and censor scenes you never got  to see in Mission Impossible 6 including  White Widow in cashmere fake trailer  shots and helicopter near collisions  spoilers ahead if you haven't seen the  movie or add this video to a watch later  playlist and come back when you're ready  one scene from the trailers which fans  were really hoping to see but which  didn't make it into the final movie was  where Ethan's helicopter was going full  pelt into an oncoming truck on a forest  road this scene would have appeared  during the already packed helicopter  chase sequence between Ethan and Henry  cavils Walker and I think could have  been during one of the moments were  Ethan's chopper was spiraling out of  control given how close the chopper and  truck come to colliding I have loved  have seen how Ethan got himself out of  this one in the movie after the halo  jump in Paris we see crews and cobble  land on the roof of the Grand Palais but  a further stunt sequence filmed inside  the Palais was Kurt the deleted scene  featured crews swinging from a rope over  the crowd and was rejected by writer  director Christopher McQuarrie because  although it looked pretty cool the film  was already running long and it wasn't  necessary for the story while the movie  gives us a number of big fight scenes  inside the Grand Palais another smaller  one this happened outside the venue was  given the chop in the final film after  ethan and white widow exit the building  next thing we know they're in the back  of a car together but there's a deleted  scene before that car ride where Ethan  gets into a fight with white widows  brother Zola and smashes his head  against a car which actually left actor  Fredrik Schmitt with a black eye  I imagine this moment was ditched in the  editing room as it didn't move the plot  forward but merely reinforced the  animosity we'd already witnessed earlier  when Zola warned Ethan not to touch his  sister actress Vanessa Kirby told MTV  that the car ride with White Widow and  Ethan was part of a much longer and now  deleted scene where in her words things  got a bit fruity between them in the  cutscene White Widow talked about how  she enjoyed having blood on her dress  from the knife fight earlier in the  parlez this deleted scene would have  further played up the flirtation between  her and Ethan and would have also been a  callback to the car ride that Ethan took  with Max in the first Mission Impossible  movie in case he missed it max was  revealed to be white widows mother in  this film and I explained that in more  detail in my Mission Impossible 6  connections and ending video this  gorgeous scene of Ethan White Widow and  Walker marching through a Hall of  Mirrors was in the movie however an  alternate shot of Ethan and Ilsa walking  down the hallway was never used  McQuarrie has said that shot of Tom  Cruise and Rebecca Ferguson was never  meant to be in the movie and was  specifically filmed as something cool  for the trailers there was also a big  fight scene with Ilsa cut from the film  and hopefully we'll get more details on  that on the blu-ray the trailers also  teased numerous shots in the final act  set in Kashmir which never made it into  the final film some of those shots hints  at some pretty dark moments with Ethan  Ilsa Benji and Luther encountering  murdered soldiers and aid workers at a  border checkpoint the scene seems to go  on with Ethan approaching the door to a  bunker opening it and descending some  stairs where I suspect he would have  discovered further horrors it's unclear  whether the murders they discover are  the actions of Walker or Solomon Lane  some Indian viewers suspect these  specific border scenes might have been  cut to avoid controversy in India as the  Kashmir region which geographically  spans India Pakistan and China is one of  the most militarized areas of the world  and has long-running border and  separatist conflicts in fact Mission  Impossible fallout has already been  censored by India's Film classification  Board or mentions of Kashmir have been  cut from the Indian release of the movie  including dialogue the title card that  comes on screen when the region first  appears and other scenes have also been  trimmed director Christopher McQuarrie  has said that any deleted trailer scenes  was simply cut because the movie was too  long which sounds perfectly reasonable  given the film's long runtime though I  wonder if in this instance political  considerations also played a part  there's some curious behind-the-scenes  footage of white widow actress Vanessa  Kirby on the set in New Zealand where  the Kashmir scenes were filmed white  widow never appeared in Kashmir in the  final film so I wonder whether there was  originally a story where the handover of  Solomon Lane that she brokered was  actually going to take place there one  of the more meta moments in Fallout  comes when  henry cavill x' walker angrily r Solomon  Lane why do you have to make everything  so complicated originally McQuarrie  planned for this line to part for much  longer segment where everything in the  movie was explained Walker's backstory  what happened to the plutonium and so on  but test audiences hated it and thought  it was tedious so it was cut I can  understand why this exposition was  removed as fans enjoyed the Mission  Impossible movies not only for their  incredible action scenes but also for  their twists and turns these work best  when the audience isn't too confused but  doesn't know everything that's going on  and so it's about getting that right  balance curiously absent from the IMF  team this time around after having  appeared in the previous two movies was  Jeremy Renner's William Brandt in an  interview with Digital Spy McQuarrie  explained that when the movie started we  didn't really have a screenplay so it  was very difficult for us to say who  would be in the movie for how long and  on what days and Renner had a commitment  to Marvel if we had a finished script we  would have been able to say yes this  will work and we can let you go for this  time but there was just no predicting  what those roles were going to turn out  to be it was just an unfortunate case of  bad timing admittedly renas role in  rogue nation was scaled back to a  smaller supporting part than the one he  had when he started the franchising  ghost Protocol so it seems natural he  would have given priority to Marvel and  of course he'd obviously have to honor  the contract he signed with them  however the worst part is as Marvel fans  know that hawkeye never even appeared in  Avengers infinity war so instead of  appearing in two of the biggest films of  2018 rena played tag with Jon Hamm Ed  Helms Hannibal Buress and Jake Johnson  instead Avengers 4 did shoot  back-to-back with infinity war though so  hopefully he does have a decent part in  that movie and assuming Renner does want  to return I think we'll see Brandt back  in Mission Impossible 7  speaking of which although I feel full  at position CIA boss Erica Sloane is the  likely successor to Handley France did  work closely with Handley in rogue  nation so it's possible he could take  over as the IMF new secretary though  that probably wouldn't be the most  interesting role for his character and  might be disappointing to fans who would  like to see him return to active duty  funny trailer moment was cut from the  scene when Benji Ethan and Luthor were  waiting to make the plutonium trade this  is a bad idea is  good one honestly so do you wish any of  these deleted scenes had been in the  film and were does fall out ranked on  your list of favorite Mission Impossible  movies let me know in the c